00:35:07.660 --> 00:35:10.830
Do you have any advice for
things to learn or technologies

00:35:10.830 --> 00:35:13.980
to learn to make yourself
more competitive in that environment

00:35:15.080 --> 00:35:17.300
and specifically in
bioscience? Sorry.

00:35:17.300 --> 00:35:17.800
- Yeah.

00:35:18.710 --> 00:35:19.370
I think--

00:35:20.030 --> 00:35:23.040
I mean, now I can only really
speak from my own company.

00:35:23.040 --> 00:35:25.520
I think there are, of course,

00:35:25.520 --> 00:35:28.680
some technologies that
we're moving more towards.

00:35:30.050 --> 00:35:31.304
So if you know

00:35:32.168 --> 00:35:34.200
any of the open
source languages--

00:35:35.750 --> 00:35:36.350
do you have--

00:35:37.970 --> 00:35:40.250
I mean, recently, when

00:35:41.030 --> 00:35:43.235
we have candidates,
we also look--

00:35:44.040 --> 00:35:47.930
are they on GitHub? Like,
have they done something interesting?

00:35:50.420 --> 00:35:53.790
Can they display a passion
for what they're doing?

00:35:53.790 --> 00:35:57.560
And for us now, we're also
putting it in our job ads that

00:35:57.560 --> 00:36:02.150
it's almost more important that you
are willing to learn new stuff.

00:36:03.440 --> 00:36:04.050
Of course,

00:36:04.050 --> 00:36:07.880
there are some jobs also in
the pharma industry where you have

00:36:07.880 --> 00:36:08.915
to have a specific

00:36:09.650 --> 00:36:13.910
degree to do that job.
But, for instance, for development jobs,

00:36:13.910 --> 00:36:15.720
we're looking much
more into that.

00:36:17.370 --> 00:36:19.830
Like, you have a
passion for doing it.

00:36:19.830 --> 00:36:22.140
We can see that you
have done it before.

00:36:22.140 --> 00:36:24.475
And when we speak with you,

00:36:25.200 --> 00:36:26.570
you know your way around,

00:36:28.920 --> 00:36:29.580
for instance,

00:36:29.580 --> 00:36:32.805
package development and
which packages you use to do

00:36:33.540 --> 00:36:34.980
package development.

00:36:36.060 --> 00:36:38.355
And so I think it's a much more

00:36:39.090 --> 00:36:41.030
now a display of interest.

00:36:41.530 --> 00:36:44.610
So I think a lot of
companies today do these

00:36:47.780 --> 00:36:48.280
interview

00:36:49.220 --> 00:36:51.605
questions or
exercises that you do

00:36:53.210 --> 00:36:54.400
before. And

00:36:55.280 --> 00:36:59.018
like if you're applying at
a pharmaceutical company, then ask

00:37:00.650 --> 00:37:03.680
about the disease that you're
maybe if you've gotten some

00:37:03.680 --> 00:37:08.000
data on some disease.
Like, what does this mean?

00:37:08.000 --> 00:37:09.530
Show that you're interested

00:37:12.701 --> 00:37:15.200
in what it is that
they are trying to

00:37:16.100 --> 00:37:17.180
do in pharma.

00:37:19.310 --> 00:37:21.170
But keeping up with

00:37:22.010 --> 00:37:23.366
technology is

00:37:25.310 --> 00:37:27.590
a really good thing to
have on your resume.

00:37:28.910 --> 00:37:29.660
- Thank you.

